<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:43:35Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Robert Pattinson: British actor will be the next James Bond</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ffeb51fcff3ec9820987b7d15c548643389efcea2c3d845277695ae3b2b5b59</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:42:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T16:39:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-robert-pattinson-british-actor-will-be-the-next-james-bond--b34bef857462.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-robert-pattinson-british-actor-will-be-the-next-james-bond" /><summary type="html">British actor Robert Pattinson is set to become the next James Bond in the long-running 007 spy franchise.
 
Discussions over the casting of the new James Bond had been going on for months, with Pattinson emerging as one of the frontrunners from the outset.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia's war on Ukraine: 'Americans want to have a deal whatever the cost for both Ukraine &amp; Europe'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c76a5c143b9d405ae4b40237bb91d4cdfbfca6b5484c6569ee2c9dddf3d1357c</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:42:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T16:22:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-s-war-on-ukraine-americans-want-to-have-a-deal-whatever-the-cost-for-both-ukraine-europe--19378cdc5fe6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-s-war-on-ukraine-americans-want-to-have-a-deal-whatever-the-cost-for-both-ukraine-europe" /><summary type="html">Delano D'Souza is pleased to welcome Grégoire Roos, Director of the Europe and Russia and Eurasia Programmes at Chatham House. As European countries prepare to take part in the next round of Ukraine peace talks, Roos questions whether having five European representatives could weaken their negotiating position. "The other option is to realize that it dilutes the negotiating power of Europe. And I would lean towards that," he says, proposing Finnish President Alexander Stubb as a possible representative. Roos also points to differences between Washington and European governments over negotiations with Russia. While "the Americans do absolutely want to have a deal whatever the cost for both Ukraine and Europe," he argues that European governments have little choice but to maintain pressure on Moscow, which has yet to abandon its "maximalist demands."</summary></entry><entry><title>Robert Pattinson named as new James Bond</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc8ad10150aee9b013af5360f1a7c0904a1a92e41bd0310d574699a69588b442</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:42:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T16:22:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-robert-pattinson-named-as-new-james-bond--8ebedea36150.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-robert-pattinson-named-as-new-james-bond" /><summary type="html">British actor ​Robert Pattinson will be the next James Bond, Amazon MGM Studios announced on Monday, ​taking on the role after Daniel Craig's departure from the long-running spy series.</summary></entry><entry><title>French film star Depardieu drops appeal against sexual conviction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b5505497fedc4746453d5a4b92839a0f7b16bf621db1d7599afcb64339c41c1</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:42:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T15:51:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-french-film-star-depardieu-drops-appeal-against-sexual-conviction--53594aa16ea5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-french-film-star-depardieu-drops-appeal-against-sexual-conviction" /><summary type="html">French film star Gérard Depardieu on Monday dropped his appeal against a conviction for sexually assaulting two women during the filming of a movie in 2021 and issued "sincere apologies" for his past behaviour on set. "For a long time on film sets, I hid behind provocation and ribald humour," Depardieu, 77, said in the statement, withdrawing his appeal on the day it was set to go to trial. "I believed my remarks and some of my gestures would be without consequences" for those involved, he said. "They were not, particularly coming from a powerful figure such as I once was."</summary></entry><entry><title>French troops in Ukraine 'wouldn't be a surprise'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1180170a50ea642c3c30ae76c1cb136bdd6a222b650c34dfbe885e3c948f26aa</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:42:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T15:49:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-french-troops-in-ukraine-wouldn-t-be-a-surprise--b8d6cfd03619.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-french-troops-in-ukraine-wouldn-t-be-a-surprise" /><summary type="html">French soldiers have been operating in Ukraine for several months, training Ukrainian troops and helping maintain military equipment, France 24's sister radio network Radio France Internationale (RFI) reported on Monday. While the deployment has not been confirmed, such a mission would not come as a surprise to many in Ukraine, reports France 24's correspondent in Kyiv Gulliver Cragg.</summary></entry><entry><title>Prague: Thousands of Czechs rally against government media funding plan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:33b4f4b55be34fe03cd573ce1e252e0e977f494ab315c729352e842f30c61df8</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:42:41Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T15:49:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-prague-thousands-of-czechs-rally-against-government-media-funding-plan--4465ea31e831.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-prague-thousands-of-czechs-rally-against-government-media-funding-plan" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of Czechs rallied in Prague on Sunday, November 15, against a government plan to cut a public media fee and move funding to the state budget, a policy critics say would dent the broadcasters' independence and viability.</summary></entry><entry><title>Robert Pattinson named as new James Bond</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:086ff03f836252f4abc99b6d0e695a7ed36aef19e9c44bb5b3fde2c2878abe95</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:42:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T15:43:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/culture/20261116-robert-pattinson-named-as-new-james-bond--2aad54206da2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/culture/20261116-robert-pattinson-named-as-new-james-bond" /><summary type="html">British actor Robert Pattinson, star of three mega-franchises, "The Batman", "Harry Potter" and "Twilight", has been named as the seventh 007. The announcement ends years of speculation about who would inherit the beloved role from Daniel Craig and comes five years after the last Bond release, "No Time to Die".</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Melissa Auf Der Maur: 90s rock memoirs and photographs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95b24e3af2496828bc96f9c9f739e44bd40c85375ec874c65fbf4a6a91876809</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:42:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T15:17:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261116-melissa-auf-der-maur-90s-rock-memoirs-and-photographs--8a62ad0e94b1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261116-melissa-auf-der-maur-90s-rock-memoirs-and-photographs" /><summary type="html">Melissa Auf Der Maur grew up in Montreal, the daughter of a feminist activist mother and a journalist-turned-politician father. At just 22, she joined Courtney Love’s band Hole as its bass player, going on to become a role model for young female fans – and not only female fans – of alternative rock. She later joined The Smashing Pumpkins before striking out on her own as a solo artist. She dropped by FRANCE 24 to talk to Marjorie Hache about the epic decade that brought the 20th century to a close.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>Verdict due in French trial over triple murder linked to Marseille drug wars</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a72b1fcabbcc6536c33477b45e772997b0ed9044b331b3fed3c74549b2340c07</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:42:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T15:13:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-verdict-due-in-french-trial-over-triple-murder-linked-to-marseille-drug-wars--011bcad14809.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-verdict-due-in-french-trial-over-triple-murder-linked-to-marseille-drug-wars" /><summary type="html">In France, a highly anticipated verdict in a triple homicide is expected later today. Often called the Kessaci trial, the plight of the Kessaci family has drawn attention across France, the surviving brother Amine Kessaci has become an outspoken advocate against drug trafficking and in particular in Marseille.</summary></entry><entry><title>Did France abandon its athletes after the Olympics?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e74c0748061dd00452b6a615f46875d2864575743dc9314ed5153b86bc631185</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:42:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T15:02:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261116-did-france-abandon-its-athletes-after-the-olympics--1308b0a82b50.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261116-did-france-abandon-its-athletes-after-the-olympics" /><summary type="html">Two years after hosting the Olympics, France seems to have lost interest in supporting its athletes. With budget cuts and lackluster interest from sponsors, some – despite their competitive successes – are turning to influencer work to finance their sport careers.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>COP31 deal draft foreshadows difficult route to consensus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca3f1a4881bc03311360c9d684ee7a9ea0829f09949769c3d2d9f228cd2cb962</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:42:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T14:56:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/environment/20261116-cop31-deal-draft-foreshadows-difficult-route-to-consensus--2f0df2694575.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/environment/20261116-cop31-deal-draft-foreshadows-difficult-route-to-consensus" /><summary type="html">COP31 negotiators in Turkey released a draft agreement on Monday to advance talks on fossil fuels and climate finance before this week's deadline. The pressure to reach a deal is intense after a year of environmental challenges including  catastrophic glacier flooding in Nepal and European wildfires, even as global conflict and cost-of-living protests distract leaders from climate action.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia dismisses commander of anti-Houthi coalition as rebels advance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eb0a54065f4358706bb9d4ec8633aa891d553634ab68e22232296b4849d70a44</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:42:59Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T14:42:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/yemen/20261116-saudi-arabia-dismisses-commander-of-anti-houthi-coalition-as-rebels-advance--f6d733473972.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/yemen/20261116-saudi-arabia-dismisses-commander-of-anti-houthi-coalition-as-rebels-advance" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia has removed the commander of the Saudi-led coalition in Yemen, state media said Monday, as the Iran-backed rebels advanced on the temporary capital of Aden. The shake up comes after Houthi forces took territory on Yemen's southern coast and Saudi-backed forces fell back to defend the capital.</summary><category term="YEMEN" /></entry><entry><title>'Historical fiction is about filling in the gaps', author Ian McGuire says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94e913a1675a6f0c0002881ff00916ebbcb84fca167d9f3d67fbbe53400be715</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:43:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T14:31:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261116-historical-fiction-is-about-filling-in-the-gaps-author-ian-mcguire-says--f87c695c3a58.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261116-historical-fiction-is-about-filling-in-the-gaps-author-ian-mcguire-says" /><summary type="html">A Man Booker Prize nominee has been speaking to FRANCE 24 about his latest novel and his passion for researching and writing historical fiction. Ian McGuire was shortlisted for the prize in 2016 for his novel “The North Water”. His latest book, “White River Crossing”, was published earlier this year and has now been translated into French, under the shortened title “White River”.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Musk among more than 150,000 calling for Jensen Huang's return to Nvidia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:175e29dfe5e7d8bc06044edfaad008a41776a28617ce3d24acad90b0734d2247</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:43:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T14:03:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-musk-among-more-than-150-000-calling-for-jensen-huang-s-return-to-nvidia--c7c573833cdd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-musk-among-more-than-150-000-calling-for-jensen-huang-s-return-to-nvidia" /><summary type="html">Could Jensen Huang make a stunning return to Nvidia just days after resigning as CEO of the AI chip giant over an affair with an alleged Chinese spy? The possibility is growing after Elon Musk and more than 158,000 others signed an open letter calling for Huang's reinstatement.</summary></entry><entry><title>French troops 'deployed in Ukraine on secret mission'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:108d060b086bdc63a6f02f7c5c2bee0f92d20342761d1b8503b0f75147bb79f0</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:43:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T14:02:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-french-troops-deployed-in-ukraine-on-secret-mission--c95d7acd52f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-french-troops-deployed-in-ukraine-on-secret-mission" /><summary type="html">French soldiers have been operating in Ukraine for several months, training Ukrainian troops and helping maintain military equipment, France 24's sister radio network Radio France Internationale (RFI) reported on Monday. France 24's Douglas Herbert takes a closer look at the report's claims.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia says intercepted over 1,300 Ukrainian drones in a major attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7fdbe6b81906b906baf7e3e27a78d88cc16efba3ece9f09859cf3bfcc393b4d2</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:43:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T14:00:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-russia-says-intercepted-over-1-300-ukrainian-drones-in-a-major-attack--3f3ce5ff4993.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-russia-says-intercepted-over-1-300-ukrainian-drones-in-a-major-attack" /><summary type="html">Russia intercepted 1,336 drones launched by Ukraine, Russia’s Defense Ministry said Monday, in what was the most claimed downings since Moscow’s all-out invasion of its neighbor nearly five years ago. Russia, meanwhile, has battered Ukrainian civilian areas with relentless strikes that seek to choke the economy and break public morale, in attacks President Volodymyr Zelensky said were made possible ⁠partly due to restrictions on Ukraine's use of SpaceX's Starshield service.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel's Netanyahu accused of electoral interference</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ecc69d9b3cd0543f26e8bff86a3aa248858dbdaaf363c5790deafd9aa4122622</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:43:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T13:58:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-israel-s-netanyahu-accused-of-electoral-interference--60e4fef31e46.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-israel-s-netanyahu-accused-of-electoral-interference" /><summary type="html">Israeli prime ministerial hopeful Gadi Eisenkot said on Sunday caretaker premier Benjamin Netanyahu must leave office immediately following reports of alleged electoral interference by a Netanyahu aide. France 24's Noga Tarnopolsky has the details.</summary></entry><entry><title>French presidential election: Should centrists hold a primary to challenge far right and left?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d4df3baeff8014e9cd6f70251bc09013cd9edd12392dec80355d37935a46377c</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:43:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T13:56:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-french-presidential-election-should-centrists-hold-a-primary-to-challenge-far-right-and-lef--5ba71ae985f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-french-presidential-election-should-centrists-hold-a-primary-to-challenge-far-right-and-left" /><summary type="html">A growing list of presidential hopefuls are jostling for attention ahead of France's 2027 election, as mainstream candidates seek to derail a showdown between the far right and far left. But with a crowded field splitting the vote, should a primary among centrist candidates? Marc Perelman takes a closer look.</summary></entry><entry><title>Iran blocks UN nuclear site visits until war ends</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6048701092cc399c0cf3d35686195022f58ee975849332f2614bf550bb1ce1ef</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:43:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T13:46:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261116-iran-blocks-un-nuclear-site-visits-until-war-ends--181a87828acf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261116-iran-blocks-un-nuclear-site-visits-until-war-ends" /><summary type="html">Iran's foreign ministry on Monday said that it would block the International Atomic Energy Agency's access to its damaged nuclear facilities until stated conditions for permanently ending the war have been met by the US. The ministry's statement follows calls for the UN watchdog to resume inspections of nuclear sites, which have been suspended since last year's 12-day war with Israel.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Excitement builds ahead of GTA VI release</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ccc559efc1904b9c3f8ea7473b1b2fca32da208ff4711ab74dddef346bf7bb4</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:43:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T13:25:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-excitement-builds-ahead-of-gta-vi-release--f38a03886ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-excitement-builds-ahead-of-gta-vi-release" /><summary type="html">After eight years of development by Rockstar Games and multiple delays, the 6th installment of the world's most talked-about game Grand Theft Auto is being released this Thursday, November 19. The game, founded nearly three decades ago and built around stealing cars and outrunning the police, boasts some 500 million sales, and this time is preparing for yet another big score, as millions of fans around the world get ready for its launch.</summary></entry><entry><title>Cape Verde President Neves wins second term</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e50035d8c5095331cd171d4fba5aa6741c73e3d8103f4c21f564a2414e6d1b5a</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:43:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T13:12:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-cape-verde-president-neves-wins-second-term--a6a7bfeca3c6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-cape-verde-president-neves-wins-second-term" /><summary type="html">Cape Verde President José Maria Neves has won a second five-year term, according to provisional results from Sunday's election, besting five challengers ​including the archipelago's ‌first female candidate after a campaign focused on the need to create more ⁠jobs for young people.</summary></entry><entry><title>Hundreds of thousands protest Czech government's media funding plan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2bf8f2c5ac708e5419b248d55dcf383b170d5713507a836dce82acc4de6f942</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:43:30Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T13:09:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-hundreds-of-thousands-protest-czech-government-s-media-funding-plan--d1e7407fcca4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-hundreds-of-thousands-protest-czech-government-s-media-funding-plan" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of thousands of Czechs rallied in Prague on Sunday against a government plan to cut a public media fee and move funding to the state budget — a policy critics say would dent the broadcasters' independence and viability.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo wraps up South America tour that tested recovery from cancer surgery</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a235d4e4be961278bc63c0c4f859e0c8673d2528a3ced37ca56b0ab75be449d7</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:43:33Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T12:15:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-pope-leo-wraps-up-south-america-tour-that-tested-recovery-from-cancer-surgery--a36125dddd11.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-pope-leo-wraps-up-south-america-tour-that-tested-recovery-from-cancer-surgery" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV concludes his 12-day homecoming tour of South America on Monday, a visit that has helped dispel concerns over his health following his recovery from cancer surgery. The 71-year-old pontiff visited Uruguay, Argentina and Peru, crisscrossing a continent where he had spent almost two decades serving as a missionary.</summary></entry><entry><title>Francophonie summit avoids 'major disaster' after clash over leadership</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d61f58f95827aa3b23006555942ee5d77be5e5079d285e66f8659a5aa6b5ffa1</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:43:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T12:13:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-francophonie-summit-avoids-major-disaster-after-clash-over-leadership--9bd9d7b546e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261116-francophonie-summit-avoids-major-disaster-after-clash-over-leadership" /><summary type="html">A summit of French-speaking nations attended by France's Emmanuel Macron postponed the election of a new chief Monday after a row between African neighbours the Democratic Republic of Congo and Rwanda. The postponement appears to have staved off a threatened walkout by DR Congo, avoiding what would have been a "major disaster", says France 24's Philip Turle.</summary></entry></feed>
